                "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
                "source": "Reference",
                "id": "Ref.4"
              }
            ],
            "value": "After 5 minutes in germination medium, detected as a soluble protein and released from apertural and non-apertural regions of pollen grain wall. In mature, non-hydrated pollen grains, predominantly associated with the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) concentric cisternae, which are situated between the vegetative nucleus and the generative cell. After 5, 15 and 30 minutes as well as 2 hours of hydration, localization to this ER region is noticeably decreased"
          }
        ]
      },
